{"id": 17, "ts": 1780460202.9119992, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I\u2019m inclined to shift my provisional recommendation to **Candidate\u202fC**.\u202fWhile we have no direct evidence of C\u2019s reliability, the facts we do have speak strongly to two of our highest\u2011priority criteria for long\u2011distance operations: stress resilience and decision quality.\u202fC \u201ckeeps calm in a crisis\u201d and \u201ccan make correct decisions quickly,\u201d which directly addresses the need for calm, effective performance under pressure and timely, safety\u2011critical judgments.\u202fAdditionally, C \u201cunderstands complicated technology,\u201d supporting the technical competence requirement.\nBy contrast, Candidate\u202fB, despite being conscientious and handling stress well, has documented \u201cnasty remarks about his colleagues\u201d and a \u201cpretentious tone,\u201d which raise serious concerns about crew cooperation and professional communication\u2014areas that can undermine cockpit resource management on long flights.\u202fWe also lack any concrete evidence that B\u2019s weak memory for numbers impacts safety, but the communication issues remain unmitigated.\nCandidate\u202fA lacks any explicit observations of reliability or stress handling (Sarah noted only unorganized behavior and poor receptiveness to criticism), and his \u201cshow\u2011off\u201d reputation and resistance to new ideas further weaken his crew\u2011cooperation prospects.\u202fCandidate\u202fD shows strong problem\u2011solving and responsibility, yet the \u201chot temper,\u201d \u201carrogant\u201d perception, and \u201cweak leadership\u201d suggest potential crew\u2011cooperation problems, with no evidence to counter that.\nGiven the balance of evidence, C\u2019s demonstrated calmness and rapid, correct decision\u2011making outweigh the communication and adaptability concerns that are less severe than B\u2019s interpersonal issues.\u202fTherefore, I recommend moving forward with Candidate\u202fC, while we continue to probe any remaining gaps in reliability and teamwork."}
